    "status": "present",
    "value": "Track shop/movie availability and rental state; return at most five cheapest available shops or rented shop/movie pairs with required tie ordering. The approach is: per-movie available heaps and global rented heap; generation stamps invalidate stale entries without duplicate reports. Its target cost is amortized O(log(E+calls)) update/heap removal, top5 query plus cleanup; O(E+calls) space. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
